  "_comment": "Every website page people can reach, with what a search engine and a share preview show for it (2026-11-07, docs/design/privacy-notice.md section 6). Data, not code: a page is a row. `node scripts/gen-page-meta.js` writes the marked block in each page's <head> from this file and data/i18n/en.json: the one-sentence description (by key, `description`), og:title (the page's own <title>), og:description, og:url (origin + path), og:type, og:image (the shared banner unless the row names a better `image`), and twitter:card. Social sites and search engines read a page's HTML without running its scripts, so the tags are written into each page rather than added by a script. scripts/tests/page-meta-web.test.js fails when an HTML file under web/ is in neither list, when a listed page lacks a title, a description or a share tag, or when a block differs from what the generator writes. A page not meant to be reached goes in `left_out` with the reason.",
